<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This download is NOT verified yet: Google publishes no hash for the file, and a check of the signature is not built, so nothing proves that the file is what Google published. The shared importer therefore refuses a real run of the cimian recipe unless the override sets cimian_allow_unverified to true (pcman_allow_unverified for the package tool's recipe). Downloads the current Google Earth Pro installer for Windows (the full, offline EXE that Google serves at a fixed address), kept under the file name of the address, and then cuts the Windows Installer database out of it with this folder's processor GoogleEarthProMsiExtractor: the EXE is a wrapper with one resource BINARY/ID_MSI, and the MSI is written beside it as googleearthprowin-x64.msi, which becomes the pathname that the importers get (they read the version from the MSI). The MSI is a part cut out of an unverified file, so it is NOT verified either. The first run under AutoPkg 2.9.0, on 2026-11-13, downloaded the file (100802200 bytes) and stopped at the earlier step WindowsExeVersion: the EXE has no version resource. 7-Zip's listing of that file showed the MSI resource; the extractor was run on a copy of it, outside AutoPkg, and wrote an MSI of 63475712 bytes that begins with the signature of a Windows Installer database. This recipe in its new form was NOT run with AutoPkg, and the MSI's ProductVersion was not read. The recipe never stops on an unchanged download, so a failed import is tried again at the next run.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.GoogleEarthPro-Win</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>GoogleEarthPro</string>
            <key>DOWNLOAD_URL</key>
            <string>https://dl.google.com/dl/earth/client/advanced/current/googleearthprowin-x64.exe</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>URLDownloader</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>url</key>
                    <string>%DOWNLOAD_URL%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>EndOfCheckPhase</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>GoogleEarthProMsiExtractor</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
